Q: Command START_REPLICATION failing while trying to conusme logical replication A: <p>tokio-postgres doesn't put the connection into replication mode by default, and even once you do, it hands you raw CopyData frames, you still have to implement the START_REPLICATION handshake, standby status/keepalive replies, and the full pgoutput message parser (Begin/Relation/Insert/Update/Delete/Commit, plus the streaming and two-phase-commitvariants) yourself. That's a lot of protocol surface to get right.</p>
<p>If you'd rather not hand-roll all of that, I maintain a crate for exactly this <a href="https://crates.io/crates/pg_walstream" rel="nofollow noreferrer">pg_walstream</a> which handles the replication connection and the pgoutput decoding.</p>
<p>GitHub Source Code : <a href="https://github.com/isdaniel/pg-walstream" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/isdaniel/pg-walstream</a></p>
<pre class="lang-rust prettyprint-override"><code>  use futures::StreamExt;

  let config = ReplicationStreamConfig::new(
      &quot;my_slot&quot;.into(),
      &quot;my_publication&quot;.into(),
      2, // pgoutput protocol version
      StreamingMode::On,
      Duration::from_secs(10),
      Duration::from_secs(30),
      Duration::from_secs(60),
      RetryConfig::default(),
  );

  // note the `?replication=database` — this is the piece that fixes your error
  let mut stream = LogicalReplicationStream::new(
      &quot;postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/mydb?replication=database&quot;,
      config,
  ).await?;

  stream.ensure_replication_slot().await?; // CREATE_REPLICATION_SLOT if missing
  stream.start(None).await?;               // issues START_REPLICATION for you

  let mut events = stream.into_stream(cancel_token);
  while let Some(result) = events.next().await {
      let event = result?;
      // ... handle the decoded change ...
      events.update_applied_lsn(event.lsn.value()); // sends standby feedback so WAL can be recycled
  }
</code></pre>
<p>The key detail for your specific error is the ?replication=database parameter on the connection string without it the server parses START_REPLICATION as a regular SQL statement, which is where your &quot;syntax error at or near START_REPLICATION&quot; comes from. It also takes care of the periodic standby status update, so the slot doesn't hold WAL forever.</p>

Q: Provider: How to notify listeners of A from B A: <p>Actually, using BuildContext as a parameter for your domain methods are not a good idea at all. It becomes impossible to test it as you cannot mock a BuildContext object and even if you do use the BuildContext inside your methods, you also need to check if the context is mounted in the widget tree, i.e., the widget is still present in the widget tree or not.</p>
<p>To solve this, you can use service locator or any way to provide dependency injection. I have used <a href="https://flutter-it.dev/documentation/get_it/getting_started" rel="nofollow noreferrer">get_It</a> service locator package for this situation. It completely detaches dependencies from your widget tree and the objects can be accessible anywhere in the app without compromising testability.</p>
<p>The way to make changes from one notifier class in another is correct the way you are doing but you just need to change the implementation of object access.</p>
<p>So, here's an example of how it would look with get_It package for Controller B class.</p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>class GameController extends ChangeNotifier {

  DrawController drawController = DrawController();

  void someFunction(BuildContext context){

     getIt&lt;DrawController&gt;().clearCanvas();//No dependency of BuildContext

   }

}
</code></pre>

Q: trying to generate a PDF and view or email it with React Native A: <pre><code>import React, { Component } from 'react';
import {
  AlertIOS,
  AppRegistry,
  StyleSheet,
  Text,
  TouchableHighlight,
  View
} from 'react-native';

import RNHTMLtoPDF from 'react-native-html-to-pdf';

export default class testApp extends Component {

 createPDF() {
    var options2 = {
    html: '&lt;h1&gt;PDF TEST&lt;/h1&gt;', // HTML String

  // ****************** OPTIONS BELOW WILL NOT WORK ON ANDROID **************                              
    fileName: 'test2',          /* Optional: Custom Filename excluded extension
                                Default: Randomly generated
                              */

    directory: 'docs',         /* Optional: 'docs' will save the file in the `Documents`
                                Default: Temp directory */

    base64: true ,               


    height: 800,                
    width: 1056,               /* Optional: 1056 sets the width of the DOCUMENT that will produced
                                Default: 792
                              */
    padding: 24,                /* Optional: 24 is the # of pixels between the outer paper edge and
                                        corresponding content edge.  Example: width of 1056 - 2*padding
                                        =&gt; content width of 1008
                                Default: 10
                              */
       };

        RNHTMLtoPDF.convert(options2).then((data2) =&gt; {
        console.log(data2.filePath);
         console.log(data2.base64);
        AlertIOS.alert(
            'options2 filename' + options2.fileName,
            'data2 filePath=' + data2.filePath
        );
    });
 }


 render() {
    return (
  &lt;View style={styles.container}&gt;
    &lt;Text style={styles.welcome}&gt;
      Welcome to testApp
    &lt;/Text&gt;

    &lt;TouchableHighlight onPress={this.createPDF}&gt;
    &lt;Text&gt;Create PDF&lt;/Text&gt;
  &lt;/TouchableHighlight&gt;

    &lt;Text style={styles.instructions}&gt;
      Press Cmd+R to reload,{'\n'}
      Cmd+D or shake for dev menu
    &lt;/Text&gt;
    &lt;/View&gt;
    );
  }
}

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    flex: 1,
   justifyContent: 'center',
 alignItems: 'center',
 backgroundColor: '#F5FCFF',
},
welcome: {
fontSize: 20,
textAlign: 'center',
margin: 10,
},
instructions: {
textAlign: 'center',
color: '#333333',
marginBottom: 5,
},
});


AppRegistry.registerComponent('testApp', () =&gt; testApp);
</code></pre>
